
1 - Read a .txt file
2 - Read the allowed alphabet from the .txt file
    and make a variable named: "ALPHABET" to store it
    // "ALPHABET" will be the characters that can be contained
    // in a password of an protected ZIP file
3 - Read the maximum number of password characters for each zip file from .txt file.
    and Make a variable named : "MAX_PASSWORD_LENGHT" to store it
    // "MAX_PASSWORD_LENGHT" will be the MAX number
    //  of posible characters in the password
4 - Read the list of ZIP files from .txt file.
    and make an array with those list of ZIP files

5 - For each ZIP file in the list:
    5.1 - Open the ZIP file.
    5.2 - For each ZIP File:
            5.2.1 - For each password length from 1 to "MAX_PASSWORD_LENGHT":
            5.2.2 - Generate all possible combinations of characters of
                    the current password length using the allowed alphabet.
            5.2.3 - Make an array of character and store all posible combinations
                    charactes made in step 5.2.2 (previous step)
            5.2.3 - For each combination of characters:
                    5.2.3.1 - Test if the combination of characters
                              can access a password-protected ZIP file
                              by using it as the password
                    5.2.3.2 - If the combination of characters in step 5.2.4.1
                              can give access to a protected ZIP file:
                              5.2.4.1 - Print the name of the ZIP file and the found
                                        password to standard output.
                              5.2.4.2 - Stop searching for passwords for the current ZIP file
                              5.2.4.3 - Continue to the next ZIP file.
    5.3 Close the ZIP file.
6 Close the program.
